 USA</source><year>2002</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>832</fpage><lpage>837</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11792868</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hiyama</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Katsura</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshihara</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishida</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinomura</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tonda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Asahara</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyagawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Haploinsufficiency of the Mus81-Eme1 endonuclease activates the intra-S-phase and G2/M checkpoints and promotes rereplication in human cells</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res.</source><year>2006</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>880</fpage><lpage>892</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16456034</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shiomi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Mori</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsuji</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Imai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Inoue</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tateishi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamaizumi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Shiomi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human RAD18 is involved in S phase-specific single-strand break repair without PCNA monoubiquitination</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res.</source><year>20